comments[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-28T03:16:17.434Z","harness:codex","Start evidence 2026-07-28: selected in a four-item managed-package SDK contract tranche after live all-status review of 2,150 items (1,835 closed, 302 open, 13 canceled, zero pre-existing in-progress), full canonical metadata/history review, and GitHub/security/dependency inventory. Only the four actively edited items are claimed and in progress."
  "2026-07-28T04:14:07.238Z","harness:codex","Implementation evidence: exported LocatedItem from the authoritative public SDK; removed package-local SDK module/type mirrors from beads, todos, templates, and governance; added a TypeScript-AST parity gate to mandatory static quality; regenerated the public SDK surface; and lowered the ESLint suppression ratchet from 132 to 131. Verification: focused linked tests passed, full typecheck/lint/contracts/SDK surfaces/token surfaces/context evaluation passed, 381 test files and 6,446 tests passed at 100/100/100/100 coverage, zero duplicate chunks, and a fresh unrelated packed consumer passed npm install, npx, bunx, package activation, runtime SDK imports, and CLI lifecycle checks."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-28T04:14:08.093Z","harness:codex",Package typechecking cannot prevent a locally copied interface from drifting when both sides compile independently. Public-surface AST conformance makes the SDK the single contract source while typeof preserves complete module shapes without handwritten signatures.
